## Keeping This Toolkit Updated

This automation package was installed from the **ai-automation-toolkit**. Improvements made there
can be pulled into this project later with one command in Copilot chat (Agent mode):

```
/sync-toolkit --source <path-to-toolkit-clone> --version <tag>
```

- `--source` is a local clone of the toolkit repository (required).
- `--version` is the toolkit release tag to update to (optional; defaults to the clone's current
  `VERSION`).
- The command has two modes, chosen automatically: **install** (first time — nothing has been
  synced into this project yet) and **update** (a previous sync is recorded in
  `.ai/.toolkit-sync-state/`). `--mode install|update` overrides the choice.
- Updates never silently overwrite customizations. Framework-only files are refreshed; files this
  project may have customized are **3-way merged** against the last synced version, and genuine
  conflicts are shown to you rather than overwritten. Project-owned files (`.ai/knowledge-base.md`,
  `.ai/data-dictionary/`) are never touched.
- The command never commits or pushes. Review the reported changes and commit them yourself.

