## 🔌 MCP Setup (Required for Full Automation)

Automatic ticket fetching and pull-request creation use MCP servers configured for your editor:

1. Install the MCP runner your team uses (for example `uvx`).
2. Generate an API token for your ticket tracker and an access credential for {{SCM_PLATFORM}}
   (for example an app password or personal access token).
3. Add both servers to `.vscode/mcp.json` using those credentials.
4. Verify in Copilot chat, for example: `@workspace Get ticket PROJ-1234 from the ticket tracker`.

GitHub Copilot CLI keeps its own MCP registry separate from `.vscode/mcp.json`; register the same
servers there if you run the workflow from the CLI. See [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) for CLI usage.

