## Troubleshooting

- **A command (`/fix-ticket`, `/fixada-*`, `/sync-toolkit`) is missing** — reload the Copilot chat
  window (or VS Code) so it re-reads `.github/prompts/`. Slash commands from `.github/prompts/`
  exist only in VS Code, not in Copilot CLI; use the `Ticket Processor` agent there instead.
- **`fix ticket` cannot fetch the ticket** — it proceeds based on the description text you pasted;
  include enough detail in `Description:`, or check your MCP configuration.
- **The workflow stops after the analysis** — you are probably in Plan or Ask mode; switch to
  Agent mode for Bug / Enhancement / CR tickets.
- **The build fails** — the workflow will not push. Fix the build (`{{BUILD_COMMAND_FULL}}`) and
  re-run; do not bypass the check.
- **Output ignores project rules or seems out of date** — confirm `.ai/knowledge-base.md` reflects
  the current code, and re-run the relevant generator from `generators/` if a config file is stale.

---

## Security

Never commit `.vscode/mcp.json` or any other file containing credentials, tokens, or app passwords
to Git — keep them out of version control (for example via `.gitignore`).
